        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T08:45:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once this is submitted, nothing releases the stream\u0027s retained buffers if the request stops reading early: e.g. JsonChildBody.toNormalizedNode never closes its reader, and ConsumableBody.close() is a no-op after consume(), so a malformed 10 MB JSON POST keeps the rest of the upload retained. Could RequestContext carry the body and requestComplete/requestFailed call body.close()? That drains the rest of the upload as DISCARDING and frees COMPLETED leftovers.",
      "revId": "972773dab40b671dd6242817386e1d63639a3a87",
